        <p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 16px;">Interconnect quality is assessed using mechanical test and inspection methods appropriate to the process.</p>
        <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 16px;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Pull and shear testing to MIL-STD-883 methods</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">X-ray on bump and joint arrays</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Post-bond AOI</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Per-unit traceability, default</span></li></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  <style>.wpr-wrap{container-type:inline-size}.wpr-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px}.wpr-card{background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);padding:14px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px}.wpr-img{height:110px;border:1px solid #EBEEF2;border-radius:6px;padding:6px;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;gap:4px;background:#fff}.wpr-img img{flex:1;min-width:0;height:100%;object-fit:contain;display:block}.wpr-n{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;color:var(--hana-blue)}.wpr-card h3{font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:16px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25;letter-spacing:-0.01em;color:var(--ink);margin:4px 0 0}.wpr-card p{font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--ink-2);margin:4px 0 0;text-wrap:pretty}.wpr-mc{margin-top:auto;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:8px;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:11px;line-height:15px;color:var(--ink)}.wpr-mc b{font-weight:600}@@container (max-width:980px){.wpr-grid{gap:8px}.wpr-card{padding:10px;gap:10px}.wpr-img{height:90px;padding:4px}.wpr-card h3{font-size:14px}.wpr-card p{font-size:11.5px}.wpr-mc{font-size:10px}}.wpr-wrap{overflow-x:auto}.wpr-grid{min-width:560px}</style><style>.ic-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-end;gap:20px 32px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:22px}.ic-fig{margin:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;flex:none}.ic-fig>div{width:240px;height:140px;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid var(--line);background:#0E1116}.ic-fig img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block}.ic-fig figcaption{font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3)}</style><div style="margin-top:48px;"><div class="ic-head"><div><h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">GGI interconnect process</h3><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:15px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:600px;margin:8px 0 0;">From gold stud bumping at wafer level through to gold-to-gold flip chip bonding, in five steps.</p></div><figure class="ic-fig"><div><img src="/images/ic-sem-stud-bumps.jpg" alt="SEM image of gold stud bumps on die pads" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption>Gold stud bumps · SEM</figcaption></figure></div><div class="wpr-wrap"><div class="wpr-grid"><div class="wpr-card"><div class="wpr-img"><img src="/images/ic-01-stud-bumping.jpg" alt="K&amp;S AT Premier Plus wafer stud bump bonder" loading="lazy"></div><div><div class="wpr-n">01</div><h3>Wafer stud bumping</h3><p>Gold stud bumps placed on the die pads at wafer level.</p></div><div class="wpr-mc"><b>K&amp;S</b><br>AT Premier Plus</div></div><div class="wpr-card"><div class="wpr-img"><img src="/images/wp-04-wafer-mounting.jpg" alt="LONGHILL LH8320 wafer mounter" loading="lazy"></div><div><div class="wpr-n">02</div><h3>Wafer mounting</h3><p>Bumped wafer mounted on dicing tape in a frame.</p></div><div class="wpr-mc"><b>LONGHILL</b><br>LH8320</div></div><div class="wpr-card"><div class="wpr-img"><img src="/images/wp-05-wafer-dicing.jpg" alt="DISCO DFD6362 dicing saw" loading="lazy"></div><div><div class="wpr-n">03</div><h3>Wafer dicing</h3><p>Precision dicing for wafers up to 12 inches.</p></div><div class="wpr-mc"><b>DISCO 12-inch</b><br>DFD6362</div></div><div class="wpr-card"><div class="wpr-img"><img src="/images/wp-06-wafer-inspection.jpg" alt="CAMTEK Eagle-i wafer inspection system" loading="lazy"></div><div><div class="wpr-n">04</div><h3>Wafer inspection</h3><p>Automated optical check of every die and bump.</p></div><div class="wpr-mc"><b>CAMTEK</b><br>Eagle-i</div></div><div class="wpr-card"><div class="wpr-img"><img src="/images/ic-05-ggi-bonding.jpg" alt="TDK AFM-1503 GGI flip chip bonder" loading="lazy"></div><div><div class="wpr-n">05</div><h3>GGI bonding</h3><p>Bumped dies flip chip bonded gold to gold.</p></div><div class="wpr-mc"><b>TDK</b><br>AFM-1503</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<div style="background:#fff;"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:44px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Why run Interconnect Solutions with Hana</h2></div><div class="why-grid"><div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;border-radius:var(--radius-panel);padding:32px 30px;background:linear-gradient(152deg,#155F9B 0%,#0E4A7C 46%,#0A3860 100%);border:none;"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;margin-bottom:22px;"><img src="/images/hana-mark-white.svg" alt="" style="width:36px;height:36px;display:block;flex:none;"><span style="flex:1;height:1px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.24);"></span></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:23px;font-weight:600;color:#fff;line-height:1.22;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0 0 12px;text-wrap:balance;">Interconnect selected around the device</h3><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:14.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.84);line-height:1.6;margin:0 0 16px;">Because Hana supports wire bond, flip chip, GGI and film bonding within the group, the interconnect process can be selected according to device performance, geometry and reliability rather than the limitations of a single assembly line.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">Method selected on engineering merit</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">Mixed methods on one assembly</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">DFM read before NPI</span></li></ul></div><div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;border-radius:var(--radius-panel);padding:32px 30px;background:linear-gradient(152deg,#FFFFFF 0%,#E5EEF5 58%,#D8E6F1 100%);border:1px solid #CBDCEA;"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;margin-bottom:22px;"><img src="/images/hana-mark.svg" alt="" style="width:36px;height:36px;display:block;flex:none;"><span style="flex:1;height:1px;background:#BFD4E4;"></span></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:23px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.22;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0 0 12px;text-wrap:balance;">Interconnect performance verified before volume</h3><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:14.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin:0 0 16px;">The selected bonding process is developed and qualified on first articles. Pull, shear, X-ray and inspection data provide documented evidence of process performance before production ramp.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #CBDCEA;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;">Method qualified on first articles</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #CBDCEA;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;">Pull, shear and X-ray data in writing</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #CBDCEA;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;">Cleanroom, ESD-controlled bonding</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #CBDCEA;border-bottom:1px solid #CBDCEA;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;">NDA signed before any die or CAD is shared</span></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div>
